===Verb===
{{wikidata lexeme|L146}}
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To assess the similarities and differences between two or more things ["to compare X with Y"]. Having made the [[comparison]] of X '''[[with]]''' Y, one might have found it [[similar]] '''[[to]]''' Y or [[different]] '''[[from]]''' Y.
#: {{syn|en|set against|weigh against|collate}}
#: {{ux|en|'''Compare''' the tiger's coloration with that of the zebra.}}
#: {{ux|en|You can't '''compare''' my problems and yours.}}
#* {{RQ:Travers Cuckoo in the Nest|chapter=6|passage=Sophia broke down here. Even at this moment she was subconsciously '''comparing''' her rendering of the part of the forlorn bride with Miss Marie Lohr's.}}
#* {{quote-journal| 1=en| year=2013| month=May-June| author=[http://www.americanscientist.org/authors/detail/katie-l-burke Katie L. Burke]| title=In the News| url=http://www.americanscientist.org/issues/pub/2013/3/in-the-news-45| volume=101| issue=3| page=193| magazine=w:American Scientist| passage=Bats host many high-profile viruses that can infect humans, including severe acute respiratory syndrome and Ebola. A recent study explored the ecological variables that may contribute to bats’ propensity to harbor such zoonotic diseases by '''comparing''' them with another order of common reservoir hosts: rodents.| archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20160222142556/http://www.americanscientist.org/issues/pub/2013/3/in-the-news-45| archivedate=22 February 2016}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To declare two things to be similar in some respect ["to compare X to Y"].
#: {{syn|en|liken}}
#: {{ux|en|Astronomers have '''compared''' comets to dirty snowballs.}}
#* {{RQ:Bacon Apophthegmes|passage=Solon '''compared''' the people unto the sea, and orators and counsellors to the winds; for that the sea would be calm and quiet if the winds did not trouble it.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=The Black Jacobins|author=C.L.R. James|page=24|edition=2nd Revised|year=1963|passage=And wordy attacks against slavery drew sneers from observers which were not altogether undeserved. The authors were '''compared''' to doctors who offered to a patient nothing more than invectives against the disease which consumed him.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|grammar}} To form the three [[degrees of comparison]] of (an adjective).
#: {{ux|en|We '''compare''' "good" as "good", "better", "best".}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To be similar (''often used in the negative'').
#: {{ux|en|A sapling and a fully-grown oak tree do not '''compare'''.}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Henry 4-2|II|iv|passage=Shall pack-horses{{...}}'''compare''' with Caesar's?}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} To [[get]]; to [[obtain]].
#* {{RQ:Spenser Faerie Queene|book=I|canto=IV|stanza=28|passage=To fill his bags, and richesse to '''compare'''.}}

